    "result": "I implemented `parse_line` in `solution.py` following the spec and wrote 41 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (41 passed). The parser walks the line once with an index: a field that starts with `\"` is read as a quoted field (doubled quotes become one quote, separators and newlines are kept, and only the separator or end of line may follow the closing quote), and any other field is read up to the next separator, raising `ValueError` on a quote or `\\r`/`\\n`. Input type and separator checks raise `TypeError` and `ValueError` as specified. The tests cover the spec examples, custom separators, quoting and whitespace rules, and every error case, and they exercise each branch of `solution.py`, so line coverage should be well above the 90% gate, though I did not run a coverage tool to confirm it.",
